THIS FILE MAKES EXPLICIT WHAT package.json ALREADY DECLARES. The manifest
says "license": "UNLICENSED", which is npm's way of saying proprietary. A
public repository with no LICENSE file sits in the same legal position by
default - absent a licence, all rights are reserved - but it leaves every
reader guessing, and some of them guess generously. This removes the guess.

IF THE INTENT IS TO OPEN-SOURCE THIS, replace this file wholesale with the
chosen licence and change the `license` field in package.json to match. The
two must agree: a repository whose manifest and LICENSE disagree is worse
than one with neither, because each reader believes whichever suits them.

Third-party components are not covered by the above and keep their own
terms. They are enumerated, with their licences, in
docs/handover/LICENCES.md - generated from the installed dependency tree
rather than maintained by hand. The bundled Anek Odia font ships under the
SIL Open Font Licence 1.1; its text is in
apps/mobile/assets/fonts/OFL-AnekOdia.txt.
